== how to read this ==
ABSENT is the reliable verdict: the vocabulary appears nowhere across 12
registry files on 2-3 independent phrasings, with four carried controls
returning non-zero in the same run. It means nobody has written the subject
down, and it is a finding.

'present' is NOT a claim that the registry carries the talking point. It
says a word appears. The registry reached these subjects by its own route
and may hold a different claim about them, a narrower one, or the opposite
one. Every 'present' row is a pointer to go and read, never a verdict that
the material is carried. The catalogue beside this file records which of
them was actually opened and what was found.
